<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01DR">Construction <span data-tag="01DR">4.5.1.1</span> <span class="named">(The Homotopy Category of $\infty $-Categories)</span>.</a> We define a category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}$ as follows: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The objects of $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}$ are $\infty $-categories. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ are $\infty $-categories, then $\operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}) = \pi _0( \operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})^{\simeq } )$ is the set of isomorphism classes of objects of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{Fun}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$ (or, equivalently, of the homotopy category $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{Fun}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$). If $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is a functor, we denote its isomorphism class by $[F] \in \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}})$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, and $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$ are $\infty $-categories, then the composition law 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \circ : \operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{} ) \times \operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{}, \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{} ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{ \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}}( \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{} )  \]
</div>
<p>
 is characterized by the formula $[G] \circ [F] = [G \circ F]$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> We will refer to $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{QCat}}$ as the <em>homotopy category of $\infty $-categories</em>. </p>
</article>
